1
00:00:00,405 --> 00:00:03,085
Picture two issues in the same
repository.

2
00:00:03,163 --> 00:00:05,296
One is about zero quantities.

3
00:00:05,374 --> 00:00:07,950
Another asks for a clearer error
message.

4
00:00:08,002 --> 00:00:10,835
The issue ID and expected behavior
change.

5
00:00:11,451 --> 00:00:15,458
The location of the test suite may stay
the same across both.

6
00:00:15,510 --> 00:00:19,256
Put recurring project conventions where
the agent can load them,

7
00:00:19,308 --> 00:00:23,142
and keep the individual issue details in
the prompt you send for that task.

8
00:00:25,076 --> 00:00:28,536
Open a Markdown template in the training
repository.

9
00:00:28,614 --> 00:00:32,926
Write a request that takes an issue and
the current source and tests as inputs.

10
00:00:33,580 --> 00:00:38,122
Ask for the proposed edit, the affected
files, and a way to verify it.

11
00:00:38,174 --> 00:00:41,036
The template should end at a plan you
can review.

12
00:00:41,140 --> 00:00:45,553
On the approved Copilot setup, paste the
filled-in text into chat to run it.

13
00:00:47,745 --> 00:00:51,517
Start Plan in the current branch and
attach the issue, validator,

14
00:00:51,569 --> 00:00:53,338
and matching test file.

15
00:00:53,417 --> 00:00:55,906
Paste the template with the issue
reference filled in.

16
00:00:56,528 --> 00:01:00,769
The response should identify the
existing comparison and explain why a

17
00:01:00,821 --> 00:01:03,007
zero test would expose it.

18
00:01:03,085 --> 00:01:05,693
Open the cited lines and check them
yourself.

19
00:01:06,342 --> 00:01:10,947
If a file name is unfamiliar, confirm it
in the workspace before accepting the

20
00:01:10,999 --> 00:01:11,461
plan.

21
00:01:13,617 --> 00:01:16,661
Open the repository root in VS Code.

22
00:01:16,739 --> 00:01:21,734
For this Copilot example, find or create
the project instructions file in the dot

23
00:01:21,787 --> 00:01:22,754
GitHub folder.

24
00:01:23,408 --> 00:01:28,481
Add the convention that unit tests use
the existing unittest suite under tests.

25
00:01:28,559 --> 00:01:32,436
Keep the rule short and include a
reliable reference for the verification

26
00:01:32,488 --> 00:01:32,987
command.

27
00:01:33,646 --> 00:01:38,055
If instructions already exist, edit the
existing guidance with your team.

28
00:01:40,242 --> 00:01:44,639
Open the agent customizations view and
find the instruction file.

29
00:01:44,717 --> 00:01:47,735
Then start a fresh chat in the same
workspace.

30
00:01:47,813 --> 00:01:51,111
Ask for a regression plan without
repeating the test convention.

31
00:01:51,749 --> 00:01:55,714
Where your client shows references,
confirm the file was included.

32
00:01:55,792 --> 00:01:58,836
Read the proposed test location and
framework.

33
00:01:58,940 --> 00:02:02,540
File discovery and correct use give you
two different things to check.

34
00:02:04,738 --> 00:02:07,626
The prompt asks for a particular piece
of work.

35
00:02:07,678 --> 00:02:11,659
The instruction file supplies reusable
project conventions.

36
00:02:11,711 --> 00:02:15,611
Required checks and actual tool
permissions enforce separate boundaries.

37
00:02:16,307 --> 00:02:20,418
Some VS Code versions also offer
runnable prompt files,

38
00:02:20,470 --> 00:02:23,410
with support depending on the selected
harness.

39
00:02:23,462 --> 00:02:26,619
The Markdown template in this example is
ready to paste.

40
00:02:27,289 --> 00:02:30,743
In the next lesson, we’ll make a
recurring procedure into a skill.

41
00:02:32,685 --> 00:02:35,755
Use the template for a second synthetic
issue.

42
00:02:35,833 --> 00:02:39,762
Swap the issue reference and attach the
current files for that task.

43
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:43,925
Compare the two plans and find one part
that changed because the requirement

44
00:02:43,977 --> 00:02:44,639
changed.

45
00:02:45,298 --> 00:02:48,342
Then find the test convention that
carried over.

46
00:02:48,420 --> 00:02:52,063
A teammate should be able to reproduce
that setup in a fresh session with the

47
00:02:52,141 --> 00:02:53,526
same project files.
